Use the following guidelines
ORGANISATIONAL ISSUES 
Critically analyse at least two contemporary organisational issues that the organisation may face or is currently facing. 
•	What is the challenge that the organisation is experiencing/may experience?
•	Why is this a major issue that needs to be addressed? 
•	How is this issue affecting the organisation?
•	Use of contemporary literature support is clear.
BUSINESS ANALYSIS TECHNIQUES
Critically apply at least two business analysis techniques to evaluate the issues.
•	What is your chosen technique to evaluate the issue? (at least 1 unique technique per issue)
•	Why have you chosen this technique to evaluate this issue?
•	Produce a table/figure of the chosen technique evaluating the issue.
•	Provide an interpretation of the findings/results. 
•	Use of contemporary literature support is clear.
SOLUTIONS 
Propose and critically justify the alignment of solutions to the issues with the organisation’s strategic goals.
•	What solution do you propose to address each issue and why?
•	How do your proposed solutions directly address the issues identified?
•	How do the solutions support or enhance the organisation’s stated or implied strategic objectives?
•	Use of contemporary literature support is clear.


